# License / SPDX snippet (drop-in examples)

Choose one license file and add a short notice in your README (or package metadata). The repository now contains LICENSE-MIT.

License badge + one-liner (example)
[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE-MIT)

One-line notice to place in your README:
License: MIT (see LICENSE-MIT)

SPDX/package metadata examples

- npm / package.json
  ```
  {
    "name": "your-package",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "license": "MIT"
  }
  ```

- NuGet / .nuspec (recommended modern approach)
  ```
  <metadata>
    ...
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
  </metadata>
  ```

- .NET SDK-style project (.csproj) for packaging
  ```
  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
  </PropertyGroup>
  ```

Notes and tips
- If you decide later to publish under CC0 instead, add LICENSE-CC0 and update the README notice.
- Include the LICENSE file in any binary distributions (e.g., in a licenses/ folder inside your ZIP or installer).
